preConditionHook:
// StopBeyondExtremeSinceBaseStart -- Grimes A list, key
// StopBeyondExtremeSinceBaseStart (G06-48): "put a stop below the lowest point
// reached while the market was in the base." Authored 2026-09-22 as a
// preEntryBars input on StopBeyondExtremeSinceEntry and split out as its own
// rule 2026-11-07, because the 202611 BRK and OWN templates place
// StopBeyondExtremeSinceEntry, so StopBeyondExtremeSinceEntry stays exactly as
// those families run it. Code otherwise unchanged. The default
// preEntryBars(10) is the miner's number; Grimes gives none.
//
// The base PREDATES the fill, so the running extreme is SEEDED from the
// preEntryBars bars before the entry bar instead of from the entry bar alone.
// Only the SEED differs from StopBeyondExtremeSinceEntry: after the fill the
// level still ratchets outward bar by bar, so a deeper pre-entry base can only
// WIDEN the stop, never tighten it. At preEntryBars 0 the seed is the fill
// bar's own extremes, the loop body never runs, and this is
// StopBeyondExtremeSinceEntry exactly.
//
// The stop sits beyond the worst price the trade has seen SO FAR, read as of
// the previous bar: the extreme through bar [1], compared against this bar's
// close. Including the current bar (the merged pseudocode's
// lowest(low, BarsSinceEntry + 1)[0]) can never fire on the long side, because
// that low is always <= this close, so the level is taken before the current
// bar is folded in.
// Running min/max rather than a window whose length is the position's age:
// same values, deepest subscript 0 instead of the longest trade.
// BarsSinceEntry() is 0 on the fill bar AND while flat, so the seed branch
// re-arms every flat bar and lands on the entry bar's own extremes.
//
// Deepest bar touched: preEntryBars.
if (el_eq((double)ctx.BarsSinceEntry(), 0.0)) {
    lowSinceEntry = low[0];
    highSinceEntry = high[0];
    for (ii = 1; ii <= (int)preEntryBars; ++ii) {
        if (el_lt(low[ii], lowSinceEntry)) lowSinceEntry = low[ii];
        if (el_gt(high[ii], highSinceEntry)) highSinceEntry = high[ii];
    }
    stopLongLevel = lowSinceEntry - ratchetOffset;
    stopShortLevel = highSinceEntry + ratchetOffset;
} else {
    stopLongLevel = lowSinceEntry - ratchetOffset;
    stopShortLevel = highSinceEntry + ratchetOffset;
    // Strict comparison, as EL's own Extremes uses: a tie keeps the earlier bar.
    if (el_lt(low[0], lowSinceEntry)) lowSinceEntry = low[0];
    if (el_gt(high[0], highSinceEntry)) highSinceEntry = high[0];
}
